  "description": "Arrow Protocol Chain Registry. v2.0 schema introduces four structured blocks per entry: protocol_required, advisory, provenance, and anchoring. The 'code' field is the canonical chain identifier and map key. Chain identifiers are distinct from the three-character canonical Origin field.",
  "v2_0_changes": [
    "Replaced flat chain_id/origin_code/chain_name/chain_trust_flag/chain_status fields with structured blocks.",
    "protocol_required: chain_trust_flag, finality_model, finality_basis_default, challenge_window_seconds, reorg_safety_confirmations, layer, settlement_chain.",
    "advisory: description, consensus, native_asset, evm_compatible.",
    "provenance: source_type, source_ref, source_version, verified_by, verified_at, review_cadence, next_review_due, notes.",
    "anchoring: entry_hash, registry_version_hash, onchain_anchor (deferred, all null).",
    "code replaces chain_id as the canonical Chain Registry identifier. It is distinct from the canonical message Origin field.",
    "Populated priority chains: ETH, BTC, SOL, BASE.",
    "Migrated ARB from v1.3 flat schema."
  ],
